  "notes": "Drawn from A321neo HL8534 (2026-06-04, right side), A350 HL8362 (2025-06-17), 777 HL7700 (2025-04-07, from below) and A330 HL8282 (2024-01-28, left side). Until about 2025 a red Kumho Asiana Group wing mark followed the title and 'KUMHO ASIANA GROUP' was lettered aft (HL8282, 2024); 2025-26 photos show neither. The aft-fuselage boundaries are measured on the A321neo and sweep forward toward the belly; the belly itself not seen squarely beyond what HL7700 shows (the colors wrap under the tail). Fin fields measured on the right side and applied mirrored (the left side faces forward the same way, HL8282). Asiana merges into Korean Air on 2026-12-17 (last Asiana-branded flights 2026-12-16); its aircraft are to be repainted into Korean Air's 2025 livery, but no schedule is published and the paint may stay for months after the merger. Re-checked 2026-11-15 on HL8534 (A321neo, the commonest type): the title starts about 2.5 m further aft than drawn (0.179, run 0.145), its cap top just under the window bottoms (cap 0.33 of the radius); the tail sweeps' edges are straight diagonals and stay as corners.",
  "history": "Replaced Skyarium v1's approximation. Introduced with Asiana's 2006 CI (replacing the 1988 gray-and-stripe scheme); to be superseded by Korean Air's 2025 livery after the December 2026 merger."
}
